  "summary": "Your messages queue is clear. All 7 refill messages (6 at the start, 1 that arrived while I worked) are decided under the refill protocol and closed. Three late results changed my earlier decisions, so two lisinopril refills were cancelled and need your review.\n\n**Frank Odum (pt-0027), lisinopril 10 mg — not refilled, needs your review**\n- At first I renewed it for 90 days with 1 refill and ordered a repeat BMP. His August potassium of 5.9 from St. Brigid was on a hemolyzed sample, so it didn't count; his last valid potassium was 4.5 in January.\n- A St. Brigid BMP drawn 10/20 then arrived on a good sample: potassium 5.8.\n- I cancelled the refill before anything was dispensed and sent you an urgent review task (task-t0020).\n- **He has no active lisinopril order right now:** the refill had replaced his old order (mr-00283), so cancelling it left nothing active. His hernia repair is now 11/12.\n- The repeat BMP order stays open. I sent him a corrected message.\n\n**Samuel Price (pt-0030)**\n- **Metformin 1000 mg twice daily:** renewed for 90 days with 1 refill. His own message and two pharmacy requests were treated as one request, with one order. His eGFR is 58 after the lab's correction (still at or above 45), and his A1c was 7.1% on 8/19 at an outside lab.\n- **Lisinopril 20 mg — not refilled, needs your review:**\n  - At first I renewed it: the 10/6 creatinine of 1.36 was 24% above his 1.10 from before the 9/18 dose increase, and potassium was 5.2.\n  - The lab then corrected that creatinine to 1.49, a 35% rise. The protocol treats a rise over 30% the same as a high potassium.\n  - I cancelled the refill and sent you an urgent review task (task-t0021).\n  - **He also has no active lisinopril order:** his 30-day order (mr-00295) was replaced the same way.\n  - I sent him a corrected message.\n\n**Marcus Webb (pt-0031)**\n- **Metformin 500 mg twice daily:** renewed for 90 days with 1 refill. I ignored the 10/14 eGFR of 39 because the lab marked it as entered in error (mislabelled sample). His eGFR is 90–92 and his A1c was 6.9% on 9/28.\n- **Lisinopril 10 mg:** renewed for 90 days with 1 refill.\n  - At first I sent only 30 days and ordered a BMP, because his last BMP (10/20/2025) was just over 12 months old.\n  - A BMP drawn 10/22 then arrived: potassium 4.6, creatinine 1.04.\n  - The BMP order I placed (sr-t0006) is now redundant, but the tools here can't cancel a lab order. I left you a routine task (task-t0032) to discontinue it. He's been told he doesn't need another blood draw for this refill.\n\nEach patient got a reply and a correction or update where it applied, and each chart has a note. I also closed the 3 new result items that came in with these patients' results.\n\n**Still open in your results queue:** 8 items for other patients, which the protocol doesn't let me act on. They include critical potassiums for pt-0016 (6.3) and pt-0008 (6.4) that need your attention.",
